WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.860
Let agents use a browser, right beside the thread.

2
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:09.672
Open Settings, Integrations, and turn on Agent browser access.

3
00:00:09.672 --> 00:00:14.980
Projects can override it, and it applies when an agent session next starts.

4
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:19.904
greet-app serves its demo page locally, on port 5173.

5
00:00:19.904 --> 00:00:22.510
Ask the coordinator to check it in the browser

6
00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.870
beside the thread, so you can watch.

7
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.192
Open the new thread.

8
00:00:28.192 --> 00:00:32.059
Its agent opens an isolated tab with the preview_* tools.

9
00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:37.154
Dock the tab beside the thread and watch it type Ada and press Greet.

10
00:00:37.154 --> 00:00:39.550
The page says Hello, Ada.

11
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.845
To try something yourself, click Take over.

12
00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:49.253
It's the same tab, and the agent waits while you drive.

13
00:00:49.253 --> 00:00:53.100
Type Grace, press Enter, then Hand back.

14
00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.169
Now ask for a screenshot.

15
00:00:55.169 --> 00:00:59.470
The agent captures the tab as you left it and shows it in the chat.

16
00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:08.830
To use your real Chrome instead, see the SpecWithCode Browser extension docs.
